I find some of them horribly obscure<p><pre><code>     +new Date() // 1259359833574
</code></pre>
Oh come on, magic constants? How do you check if that's the right number?<p><pre><code>    function PrefixInteger(num, length) {

        return (num / Math.pow(10, length)).toFixed(length).substr(2);
     }
</code></pre>
Is there no sprintf in Javascript? Or did I misunderstand what the function does?
